 },
 "sprite_review": {
  "score": 6.0,
  "problems": [
   "At a glance, beside the person, it reads more like a white filing cabinet or a small chest of drawers than a beehive. That's because of the flat white paint, the two drawer-like handgrip slots and the plain grey lid.",
   "It isn't wooden. The brief asks for a wooden box hive and the spec says natural wood, but the boxes are painted bright white. That is also the brightest thing in the scene, which goes against the house palette of charcoal, brushed metal and gold.",
   "It has only two stacked boxes, but the spec says three supers.",
   "There are no bees around it. A few specks sit on the landing board in the 'alone' view, and they disappear entirely at scene scale. The brief needs bees flying near the hive.",
   "The entrance slot is a dark strip low on the base, and it doesn't read as a hive entrance at scene size."
  ]
 }
}